{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "history-circa-summer-1832", "page": "2", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_001_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "1", "href": "/paper-summary/history-circa-summer-1832/1"}, {"image": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_002_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "2", "href": "/paper-summary/history-circa-summer-1832/2"}, {"image": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_003_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "3", "href": "/paper-summary/history-circa-summer-1832/3"}, {"image": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_004_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "4", "href": "/paper-summary/history-circa-summer-1832/4"}, {"image": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_005_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "5", "href": "/paper-summary/history-circa-summer-1832/5"}, {"image": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_006_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "[6]", "href": "/paper-summary/history-circa-summer-1832/6"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "history-circa-summer-1832", "series": "JSPPH", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPH1", "documentSeriesTitle": "History, circa Summer 1832", "editorialPageNumber": "2", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26015/26015-0002.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"><span class=\"josephswriting\"> with regard to the all importent concerns </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> for the well</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">fare of my immortal Soul which led me to search</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ing the scriptures believeing as I was taught, that </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">they contained the word of God thus applying </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">myself to them and my intimate acquaintance </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">with those of differant denominations led me to </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">marvel excedingly for I discovered that </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">they did not </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">adorn</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> their profession by a holy walk and God</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ly conversation</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5469645757962578691\"><a href=\"#5469645757962578691\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 1 Peter 1:15; 2 Peter 3:11; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/articles-and-covenants-circa-april-1830-dc-20\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/articles-and-covenants-circa-april-1830-dc-20\" poptitle=\"Articles and Covenants, circa April 1830\n[D&amp;C 20]\">Articles and Covenants, ca. Apr. 1830</a> [D&amp;C 20:69].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> agreeable to what I found contain</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ed in that sacred depository this was a grief to </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">my Soul thus from the age of twelve years </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">to fifteen I pondered many things in my heart </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">concerning the sittuation of the world of mankind </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the contentions and divi</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">si</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ons the wicke</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">d</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ness and </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">abominations and the darkness which pervaded </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> minds of mankind my mind become </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">excedingly distressed for I become convicted of my </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">sins and by searching the scriptures I found </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">that </span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">mankind</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> did not come unto the Lord but that </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">they had apostatised from the true and liveing </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">faith and there was no society or denomination </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">that built upon the gospel of Jesus Christ as </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">recorded in the new testament</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10924800321802094834\"><a href=\"#10924800321802094834\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Like the Disciples of Christ and other primitivists, JS believed that the mainline churches of his day had strayed from the order and teachings of the New Testament church. (See Hughes and Allen, <span class=\"title\">Illusions of Innocence,</span> chap. 6.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Hughes, Richard T., and C. Leonard Allen. <span class=\"title\">Illusions of Innocence: Protestant Primitivism in America, 1630–1875.</span> Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 1988. </p></div></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> and I felt to mourn </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">for my own sins and for the sins of the world</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7650515946140643208\"><a href=\"#7650515946140643208\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See, for example, 1 John 2:2; and Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=524\" class=\"externalLink\">518</a> [4 Nephi 1:44].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">for I learned in the scriptures that God was </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the same yesterday to day and forever</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11350719446274054401\"><a href=\"#11350719446274054401\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans11\"><span id=\"documenttrans11\">11</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Hebrews 13:8; and Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=117\" class=\"externalLink\">111</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=122\" class=\"externalLink\">116</a> [2 Nephi 27:23; 29:9].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> that he was </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">no respecter to persons</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10883785072364464388\"><a href=\"#10883785072364464388\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans12\"><span id=\"documenttrans12\">12</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Acts 10:34–35; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-1-november-1831-b-dc-1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-1-november-1831-b-dc-1\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 1\nNovember 1831–B [D&amp;C 1]\">Revelation, 1 Nov. 1831–B</a> [D&amp;C 1:35]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-january-1831-dc-38\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-january-1831-dc-38\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 2 January 1831 [D&amp;C\n38]\">Revelation, 2 Jan. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 38:16].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> for he was God for I </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">looked upon the sun the glorious luminary of </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the earth and also the moon rolling in their </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">magesty through the heavens and also the stars </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">shining in their courses and the earth also upon whic</span><span class=\"josephswriting\">h I stood and the beast of the field and the fowls of </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">heaven and the fish of the waters and also man walking </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">forth upon the face of the earth in magesty and in </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the strength of beauty whose power and intiligence </span><span class=\"josephswriting\">in governing the things which are so exceding great and </span> [p. 2]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"><span class=\"josephswriting\"> with regard to the all importent concerns </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">of</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> for the well</span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">fare of my immortal Soul which led me to search</span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ing the scriptures believeing as I was taught, that </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">they contained the word of God thus applying </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">myself to them and my intimate acquaintance </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">with those of differant denominations led me to </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">marvel excedingly for I discovered that </span>&lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">they did not </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">adorn</span></span>​&gt;<span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">instead of</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">adorn</span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">ing</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> their profession by a holy walk and God</span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ly conversation</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10845494131518261613\"><a href=\"#10845494131518261613\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 1 Peter 1:15; 2 Peter 3:11; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/articles-and-covenants-circa-april-1830-dc-20\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/articles-and-covenants-circa-april-1830-dc-20\" poptitle=\"Articles and Covenants, circa April 1830\n[D&amp;C 20]\">Articles and Covenants, ca. Apr. 1830</a> [D&amp;C 20:69].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> agreeable to what I found contain</span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">ed in that sacred depository this was a grief to </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">my Soul thus from the age of twelve years </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">to fifteen I pondered many things in my heart </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">concerning the sittuation of the world of mankind </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the contentions and divi</span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">si</span>]<span class=\"josephswriting\">ons the wicke</span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">d</span>]<span class=\"josephswriting\">ness and </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">abominations and the darkness which pervaded </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">of the</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> minds of mankind my mind become </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">excedingly distressed for I become convicted of my </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">sins and by searching the scriptures I found </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">that </span><span class=\"deleted\"><span class=\"josephswriting\">mand</span></span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>&lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">mankind</span>​&gt;<span class=\"josephswriting\"> did not come unto the Lord but that </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">they had apostatised from the true and liveing </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">faith and there was no society or denomination </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">that built upon the gospel of Jesus Christ as </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">recorded in the new testament</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13752038714977490172\"><a href=\"#13752038714977490172\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Like the Disciples of Christ and other primitivists, JS believed that the mainline churches of his day had strayed from the order and teachings of the New Testament church. (See Hughes and Allen, <span class=\"title\">Illusions of Innocence,</span> chap. 6.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Hughes, Richard T., and C. Leonard Allen. <span class=\"title\">Illusions of Innocence: Protestant Primitivism in America, 1630–1875.</span> Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 1988. </p></div></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> and I felt to mourn </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">for my own sins and for the sins of the world</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7126655793767336470\"><a href=\"#7126655793767336470\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans10\"><span id=\"documenttrans10\">10</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See, for example, 1 John 2:2; and Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=524\" class=\"externalLink\">518</a> [4 Nephi 1:44].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">for I learned in the scriptures that God was </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the same yesterday to day and forever</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10374789923592860916\"><a href=\"#10374789923592860916\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans11\"><span id=\"documenttrans11\">11</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Hebrews 13:8; and Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=117\" class=\"externalLink\">111</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=122\" class=\"externalLink\">116</a> [2 Nephi 27:23; 29:9].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> that he was </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">no respecter to persons</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9072050288788683322\"><a href=\"#9072050288788683322\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans12\"><span id=\"documenttrans12\">12</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Acts 10:34–35; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-1-november-1831-b-dc-1\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-1-november-1831-b-dc-1\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 1\nNovember 1831–B [D&amp;C 1]\">Revelation, 1 Nov. 1831–B</a> [D&amp;C 1:35]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-january-1831-dc-38\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-january-1831-dc-38\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 2 January 1831 [D&amp;C\n38]\">Revelation, 2 Jan. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 38:16].</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> for he was God for I </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">looked upon the sun the glorious luminary of </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the earth and also the moon rolling in their </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">magesty through the heavens and also the stars </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">shining in their courses and the earth also upon whic</span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">h I stood and the beast of the field and the fowls of </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">heaven and the fish of the waters and also man walking </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">forth upon the face of the earth in magesty and in </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">the strength of beauty whose power and intiligence </span><span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"josephswriting\">in governing the things which are so exceding great and </span> [p. 2]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_002_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_002_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_002.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_002_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/6547/6547_ms155_2_01_lb1_history_002.xml", "classification": "Histories", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "6547", "requestedPageNumber": "2", "numberOfPages": "6", "editorialTitle": "History, circa Summer 1832", 